IMPORT prelude

-- Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003 (Singapore) -- unfair practices and the consumer's own action for them: who is a
-- consumer and a supplier (s 2), what is a consumer transaction (s 2, First Schedule), when Part 2 reaches a dealing (s 3), what is an
-- unfair practice (s 4, Second Schedule paras 10, 25, 26, 27 worked out from facts, the rest taken as a fact), acts of employees and
-- agents (s 5(3)(b)), the consumer's right to sue and its money limit (s 6(1) to (6)), the Small Claims Tribunal's jurisdiction
-- (s 7(1), (2)), no relief for business use (s 7(7) to (9)), the time limit (s 12(1)), no contracting out (s 35), heirs and assignees
-- (s 36), spoken warranties (s 39) and ambiguous documents (s 40).
--
-- SEAT: the consumer -- the individual who bought, hired, was given or won goods or services from a business and asks what the Act
-- gives them. Every decision is phrased as the consumer would ask it, on facts the consumer could state.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 9 March 2025 (SSO "Current version as at 30 Sep 2026"),
-- as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CPFTA2003.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Part 3 (non-conforming goods) is in cpfta-defective-goods.l4. Out here: voluntary compliance agreements (s 8, except
-- as noted), the Commission's declarations and injunctions (ss 9, 10), cancellation (s 11: nothing is cancellable until regulations
-- name a class of contracts, and none is deposited), the Commission's investigation powers and the offences (Parts 3A, 3B), the
-- stay and discontinuance of an action (s 6(7) to (9)), the court's list of orders (s 7(5)), the dispute-resolution factor
-- (s 7(10), (11)), publishers (s 38), burden of proof (s 41: no regulations specifying the requirements are deposited), the
-- Fourth Schedule's disability extension, the Fifth Schedule, and the machinery (ss 42 to 44). Second Schedule paras 1 to 9, 11 to 24
-- are asked as one fact. A Minister's order changing the $30,000 limit (s 6(6)) is not deposited; the Act's own figure is used.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual to
-- whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass,
-- no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003 -- unfair practices`

§§ `2(1), (2) -- consumer and supplier`

-- "consumer" means "an individual who, otherwise than exclusively in the course of business -- (a) receives or has the right to
-- receive goods or services from a supplier; or (b) has a legal obligation to pay a supplier for goods or services that have been or
-- are to be supplied to another individual". s 2(2): one who "holds himself or herself out as acting exclusively in the course of
-- business is treated as" so acting.
DECLARE `My position` HAS
    `I am an individual`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `I acted exclusively in the course of business`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `I held myself out as acting exclusively in the course of business`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `I receive or have the right to receive the goods or services`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `I must pay for goods or services supplied to another individual`        IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN me IS A `My position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a consumer` IF
        me's `I am an individual`
    AND NOT me's `I acted exclusively in the course of business`
    AND NOT me's `I held myself out as acting exclusively in the course of business`
    AND (   me's `I receive or have the right to receive the goods or services`
         OR me's `I must pay for goods or services supplied to another individual`)

-- "supplier" means "a person who, in the course of the person's business -- (a) provides goods or services to consumers; (b)
-- manufactures, assembles or produces goods; (c) promotes the use or purchase of goods or services; or (d) receives or is entitled
-- to receive money or other consideration as a result of the provision of goods or services to consumers, and includes any employee
-- or agent of the person".
DECLARE `The other side` HAS
    `it acted in the course of its business`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `it provides goods or services to consumers`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `it manufactures or assembles or produces goods`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `it promotes the use or purchase of goods or services`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is paid as a result of goods or services provided to consumers`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is an employee or agent of a supplier`                               IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN them IS A `The other side`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the other side a supplier` IF
        them's `it is an employee or agent of a supplier`
    OR  (    them's `it acted in the course of its business`
         AND (   them's `it provides goods or services to consumers`
              OR them's `it manufactures or assembles or produces goods`
              OR them's `it promotes the use or purchase of goods or services`
              OR them's `it is paid as a result of goods or services provided to consumers`))

§§ `2(1) and First Schedule -- consumer transaction`

-- "consumer transaction" means "(a) the supply of goods or services by a supplier to a consumer as a result of a purchase, lease,
-- gift, contest or other arrangement; or (b) an agreement ... in which the supplier is to supply goods or services", "but does not
-- include any transaction specified in the First Schedule". First Schedule para 1: "(a) acquisition of an estate or interest in any
-- immovable property (but not including any lease of residential property granted in consideration of rent or any time share
-- contract); (b) (to avoid doubt) service provided under a contract of employment."
-- "goods" includes "any residential property" (and one "in the course of being constructed"), yet buying it is an acquisition of an
-- interest in immovable property and so is excluded; renting it is not.
DECLARE `My dealing` HAS
    `it is a supply or agreement to supply goods or services to me`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is the acquisition of an estate or interest in immovable property`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a lease of residential property granted for rent`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a time share contract`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is service under a contract of employment`                           IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN dealing IS A `My dealing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my dealing a consumer transaction` IF
        dealing's `it is a supply or agreement to supply goods or services to me`
    AND NOT `it is an excluded immovable property acquisition`
    AND NOT dealing's `it is service under a contract of employment`
  WHERE
    `it is an excluded immovable property acquisition` MEANS
            dealing's `it is the acquisition of an estate or interest in immovable property`
        AND NOT dealing's `it is a lease of residential property granted for rent`
        AND NOT dealing's `it is a time share contract`

§§ `3 -- does Part 2 reach my dealing`

-- "This Part does not apply unless -- (a) the supplier or consumer is resident in Singapore; or (b) the offer or acceptance relating
-- to the consumer transaction is made in or is sent from Singapore."
GIVEN `the supplier is resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `I am resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `the offer or acceptance was made in or sent from Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does Part 2 reach my dealing` IF
        `the supplier is resident in Singapore`
    OR  `I am resident in Singapore`
    OR  `the offer or acceptance was made in or sent from Singapore`

§§ `4 and Second Schedule -- unfair practice`

-- s 4: "It is an unfair practice for a supplier, in relation to a consumer transaction -- (a) to do or say anything, or omit to do or
-- say anything, if as a result a consumer might reasonably be deceived or misled; (b) to make a false claim; (c) to take advantage of
-- a consumer if the supplier knows or ought reasonably to know that the consumer -- (i) is not in a position to protect his or her
-- own interests; or (ii) is not reasonably able to understand the character, nature, language or effect of the transaction ...; or
-- (d) ... to do anything specified in the Second Schedule."
-- Second Schedule para 10: "Charging a price ... substantially higher than an estimate provided to the consumer, except where the
-- consumer has expressly agreed to the higher price in advance." Para 25: "Purporting to assert a right to payment for the supply of
-- unsolicited goods or services." Para 26: an invoice for unsolicited goods or services without, as its most prominent text, "This
-- is not a bill. You are not required to pay any money." (or words to that effect), "unless the consumer has expressly acknowledged
-- to the supplier in writing the consumer's intention to accept and pay". Para 27: where an "applicable agreement" was made in
-- writing and no copy given, "refusing to give the consumer a copy ... upon the consumer's request".
-- Part 2 para 1(a): "unsolicited goods or services" are those supplied "to a consumer who did not request them". Para 2: a request
-- or an intention to pay "is not to be inferred only from the consumer's -- (a) payment ...; (b) use of, dealing with or disposal of
-- the goods or services; (c) request to purchase another similar good or service; or (d) inaction." Para 3: an "applicable
-- agreement" expressly provides that nothing is supplied (or begins to be supplied) until the price or part of it is paid, and that
-- the price is paid "by 2 or more instalments"; "any deposit paid by the consumer ... is treated as an instalment".
-- Not encoded: para 1(a)'s goods meant for another person, and para 1(b)'s material change in a continuing supply.
DECLARE `What the supplier did` HAS
    `I might reasonably have been deceived or misled by it`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supplier made a false claim`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supplier took advantage of me`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supplier knew or ought to have known I could not protect my own interests` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supplier knew or ought to have known I could not understand the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is another practice listed in the Second Schedule`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the price charged was substantially higher than the estimate given to me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I expressly agreed to the higher price in advance`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `I requested the goods or services`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `I paid for or used the goods or services`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supplier asserted a right to payment for them`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supplier sent me an invoice for them`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the invoice's most prominent text says it is not a bill`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `I acknowledged in writing that I intended to accept and pay`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement says nothing is supplied until some of the price is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `number of instalments counting any deposit`                             IS A NUMBER
    `the agreement was made in writing`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was given a copy of the agreement`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supplier refused my request for a copy`                             IS A BOOLEAN

-- Para 2: paying for or using the goods is not a request. The field `I paid for or used the goods or services` is read by nothing,
-- deliberately: that is what para 2 says.
GIVEN act IS A `What the supplier did`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Were the goods or services unsolicited` IF
    NOT act's `I requested the goods or services`

GIVEN act IS A `What the supplier did`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the supplier do something listed in the Second Schedule` IF
        act's `it is another practice listed in the Second Schedule`
    OR  `para 10 -- price substantially above the estimate`
    OR  `para 25 -- demanding payment for unsolicited goods or services`
    OR  `para 26 -- an invoice for them without the not-a-bill notice`
    OR  `para 27 -- refusing a copy of an applicable agreement`
  WHERE
    `para 10 -- price substantially above the estimate` MEANS
            act's `the price charged was substantially higher than the estimate given to me`
        AND NOT act's `I expressly agreed to the higher price in advance`
    `para 25 -- demanding payment for unsolicited goods or services` MEANS
            `Were the goods or services unsolicited` act
        AND act's `the supplier asserted a right to payment for them`
    `para 26 -- an invoice for them without the not-a-bill notice` MEANS
            `Were the goods or services unsolicited` act
        AND act's `the supplier sent me an invoice for them`
        AND NOT act's `the invoice's most prominent text says it is not a bill`
        AND NOT act's `I acknowledged in writing that I intended to accept and pay`
    `it is an applicable agreement` MEANS
            act's `the agreement says nothing is supplied until some of the price is paid`
        AND act's `number of instalments counting any deposit` AT LEAST 2
    `para 27 -- refusing a copy of an applicable agreement` MEANS
            `it is an applicable agreement`
        AND act's `the agreement was made in writing`
        AND NOT act's `I was given a copy of the agreement`
        AND act's `the supplier refused my request for a copy`

GIVEN act IS A `What the supplier did`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the supplier engaged in an unfair practice` IF
        act's `I might reasonably have been deceived or misled by it`
    OR  act's `the supplier made a false claim`
    OR  (    act's `the supplier took advantage of me`
         AND (   act's `the supplier knew or ought to have known I could not protect my own interests`
              OR act's `the supplier knew or ought to have known I could not understand the transaction`))
    OR  `Did the supplier do something listed in the Second Schedule` act

§§ `5(3)(b) -- acts of employees and agents`

-- "an act or omission by an employee or agent of a person is deemed also to be an act or omission of the person if the act or
-- omission occurred in the course of -- (i) the employee's employment with the person; or (ii) the agent exercising the powers or
-- performing the duties on behalf of the person within the scope of the agent's actual or apparent authority."
GIVEN `the supplier did it itself` IS A BOOLEAN, `its employee did it in the course of employment` IS A BOOLEAN, `its agent did it within actual or apparent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what was done to me the supplier's own act` IF
        `the supplier did it itself`
    OR  `its employee did it in the course of employment`
    OR  `its agent did it within actual or apparent authority`

§§ `6(2) to (6) -- the money limit on my action`

-- s 6(2): the right to sue "does not apply where -- (a) the amount of the claim exceeds the prescribed limit; or (b) there is no claim
-- for money, and the remedy or relief sought ... is in respect of a subject matter the value of which exceeds the prescribed limit."
-- (3): a balance not exceeding the limit "after set-off ... admitted by the consumer in the particulars of his or her claim" does not
-- exceed it. (5): the consumer "may abandon the excess", and then "must not recover in that action an amount exceeding the prescribed
-- limit". (6): "The prescribed limit mentioned in this section is $30,000 or any other amount that the Minister may, by order in the
-- Gazette, prescribe." No such order is deposited.
`the prescribed limit` MEANS 30000

DECLARE `My claim` HAS
    `I claim money`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount I claim`                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `the set-off I admit in my particulars`                                  IS A NUMBER
    `I abandon the excess over the limit`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the value of the subject matter`                                        IS A NUMBER

GIVEN claim IS A `My claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my claim within the prescribed limit` IF
    IF   claim's `I claim money`
    THEN     `the balance after admitted set-off` AT MOST `the prescribed limit`
         OR  claim's `I abandon the excess over the limit`
    ELSE claim's `the value of the subject matter` AT MOST `the prescribed limit`
  WHERE
    `the balance after admitted set-off` MEANS claim's `the amount I claim` MINUS claim's `the set-off I admit in my particulars`

-- NOTHING where the claim is outside s 6 altogether, or is not a claim for money (s 6 caps no non-money relief by amount).
GIVEN claim IS A `My claim`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most I can recover in my action` MEANS
    IF   (NOT claim's `I claim money`) OR (NOT `Is my claim within the prescribed limit` claim)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (min `the balance after admitted set-off` `the prescribed limit`)
  WHERE
    `the balance after admitted set-off` MEANS claim's `the amount I claim` MINUS claim's `the set-off I admit in my particulars`

-- s 6(4): where the subject matter is a residential property its value is "(a) the annual value ... appearing in the Valuation List
-- ...; (b) the annual rent, or 12 times the monthly rent, payable by the tenant ... (if this value is lower than the value in
-- paragraph (a)); or (c) if the annual value, annual rent or monthly rent cannot be ascertained, one-tenth of the last transacted
-- price." Read: (c) applies when none of the three can be ascertained.
-- NOT COVERED: an annual rent or monthly rent is known but no annual value. (b) takes the rent only "if this value is lower than the
-- value in paragraph (a)", and there is nothing to compare it with; the text does not say. The answer is NOTHING.
GIVEN `the annual value` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the annual rent` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the monthly rent` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the last transacted price` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is my home worth for the limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the annual value`
    WHEN JUST av THEN
        CONSIDER `the rent`
        WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (min av r)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST av
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `the rent`
        WHEN JUST r THEN NOTHING
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (`the last transacted price` DIVIDED BY 10)
  WHERE
    `the rent` MEANS
        CONSIDER `the annual rent`
        WHEN JUST ar THEN JUST ar
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            CONSIDER `the monthly rent`
            WHEN JUST mr THEN JUST (12 TIMES mr)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `12(1) -- the time limit on my action`

-- "No action under section 6 may be commenced later than 2 years after -- (a) the date of the occurrence of the last material event
-- on which the action is based; or (b) the earliest date on which the consumer had knowledge that the supplier had engaged in the
-- unfair practice ..., whichever occurs later." (7): knowledge "includes knowledge which he or she might reasonably have been expected
-- to acquire" from observable facts or reasonable expert advice; (6): knowing that it was, in law, an unfair practice is irrelevant.
-- "2 years after" a 29 February is taken as 28 February (an inference; the text does not say). Commencing on the last day is in time
-- ("later than"). The Fourth Schedule's extension for a consumer under a disability is not encoded.
GIVEN d IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days in the month reached` MEANS
    IF   m EQUALS 2
    THEN IF   `leap` THEN 29 ELSE 28
    ELSE IF   m EQUALS 4 OR m EQUALS 6 OR m EQUALS 9 OR m EQUALS 11
         THEN 30
         ELSE 31
  WHERE
    total MEANS DATE_MONTH d MINUS 1 PLUS n
    y MEANS DATE_YEAR d PLUS FLOOR (total DIVIDED BY 12)
    m MEANS total MINUS 12 TIMES FLOOR (total DIVIDED BY 12) PLUS 1
    `leap` MEANS (y MODULO 4 EQUALS 0 AND (NOT (y MODULO 100 EQUALS 0))) OR y MODULO 400 EQUALS 0

-- The date n calendar months after d, a day that does not exist in the month reached falling back to that month's last day.
GIVEN d IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`months after` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY d) (`days in the month reached` d n)) m y
  WHERE
    total MEANS DATE_MONTH d MINUS 1 PLUS n
    y MEANS DATE_YEAR d PLUS FLOOR (total DIVIDED BY 12)
    m MEANS total MINUS 12 TIMES FLOOR (total DIVIDED BY 12) PLUS 1

GIVEN `the last material event` IS A DATE
      `the earliest date I knew or reasonably could have known of the practice` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day I can start my action` MEANS
    `months after` `the later date` 24
  WHERE
    `the later date` MEANS
        CONSIDER `the earliest date I knew or reasonably could have known of the practice`
        WHEN JUST k THEN IF   DATE_SERIAL k GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the last material event`
                         THEN k
                         ELSE `the last material event`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the last material event`

GIVEN `the last material event` IS A DATE
      `the earliest date I knew or reasonably could have known of the practice` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date I start my action` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in time to sue under section 6` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the date I start my action` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL (`What is the last day I can start my action` `the last material event` `the earliest date I knew or reasonably could have known of the practice`)

§§ `6(1) -- can I sue the supplier`

-- "A consumer who has entered a consumer transaction involving an unfair practice may commence an action in a court of competent
-- jurisdiction against the supplier", subject to the limit (s 6(2)) and the time bar (s 12(1)); Part 2 must reach the dealing (s 3).
GIVEN `I am a consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other side is a supplier` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a consumer transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Part 2 reaches it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supplier engaged in an unfair practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my claim is within the limit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I sue the supplier for an unfair practice` IF
        `I am a consumer`
    AND `the other side is a supplier`
    AND `it is a consumer transaction`
    AND `Part 2 reaches it`
    AND `the supplier engaged in an unfair practice`
    AND `my claim is within the limit`
    AND `I am in time`

§§ `7(1), (2) -- can a Small Claims Tribunal hear it`

-- s 7(1): a Small Claims Tribunal "has jurisdiction to hear and determine -- (a) any action under section 6(1) insofar as the action
-- relates to an unfair practice involving a relevant contract; ... (e) any action insofar as it relates to a deposit paid in relation
-- to or in contemplation of a motor vehicle sale contract." (2): "relevant contract" means a contract in "paragraph 1(a) or (c) of the
-- Schedule to the Small Claims Tribunals Act 1984, but does not include a contract relating to the sale of immovable property".
-- The Small Claims Tribunals Act is not deposited: whether the contract is in that Schedule is asked as a fact, and the Tribunal's own
-- money limits (s 7(3)) are not encoded. Paras (b) to (d) are not encoded.
GIVEN `my contract is in paragraph 1(a) or (c) of the Small Claims Tribunals Act Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my contract relates to the sale of immovable property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my claim relates to a deposit for a motor vehicle sale contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a Small Claims Tribunal hear my claim` IF
        (    `my contract is in paragraph 1(a) or (c) of the Small Claims Tribunals Act Schedule`
         AND NOT `my contract relates to the sale of immovable property`)
    OR  `my claim relates to a deposit for a motor vehicle sale contract`

§§ `7(7) to (9) -- goods or services I meant for business use`

-- (7): "the court is not to grant any relief in respect of any goods or services intended for business use in an action under section
-- 6(1)". (8): the court "may apportion the use ... between business use and non-business use as the court considers just and
-- equitable ... and grant relief only in respect of the portion ... attributed with non-business use". (9): business use includes
-- goods or services "the consumer intends to resell in the course of his or her business" and goods the consumer "intends to use up
-- or transform, in the course of his or her business, in a process of production or manufacturing or in repairing or treating other
-- goods or fixtures".
DECLARE `Relief for my goods or services` IS ONE OF
    `relief may be granted`
    `no relief -- intended for business use`
    `relief only for the part the court attributes to non-business use`

GIVEN `I intend them only for business use` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I intend them partly for business use` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I intend to resell them in my business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I intend to use them up or transform them in my business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Relief for my goods or services`
`What relief can I get for goods or services I meant for business use` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `I intend them only for business use`
            OR `I intend to resell them in my business`
            OR `I intend to use them up or transform them in my business`
        THEN `no relief -- intended for business use`
        IF `I intend them partly for business use`
        THEN `relief only for the part the court attributes to non-business use`
        OTHERWISE `relief may be granted`

§§ `35 -- can the contract take my rights away`

-- (1): the Act prevails "despite any agreement to the contrary and any term contained in a contract is void, if and to the extent that
-- it is inconsistent with the provisions of this Act." (2): "Any waiver or release given of any right, benefit or protection conferred
-- under this Act is void." (3): (1) and (2) "do not apply to any release made by a person in settlement of a dispute."
GIVEN `the term or waiver cuts down a right the Act gives me` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is a release I made in settlement of a dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I bound by the term or waiver` IF
        NOT `the term or waiver cuts down a right the Act gives me`
    OR  `it is a release I made in settlement of a dispute`

§§ `36 -- heirs and assignees`

-- "Where, other than in the course of business, an individual, as heir or assignee of a consumer, receives goods or services, that
-- individual has the same rights as the consumer to seek and obtain redress from the supplier under this Act."
GIVEN `I am an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `I am the consumer's heir or assignee` IS A BOOLEAN, `I received the goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN, `I received them in the course of business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have the consumer's rights as heir or assignee` IF
        `I am an individual`
    AND `I am the consumer's heir or assignee`
    AND `I received the goods or services`
    AND NOT `I received them in the course of business`

§§ `39, 40 -- warranties outside the paper, and ambiguous documents`

-- s 39(1): "parol or extrinsic evidence establishing the existence of an express warranty is admissible in any action relating to a
-- consumer transaction ... even though it adds to, varies or contradicts a written contract." (2): not "in respect of goods or services
-- intended for business use".
GIVEN `it is an action about a consumer transaction` IS A BOOLEAN, `the goods or services were intended for business use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I prove a warranty that is not in the written contract` IF
        `it is an action about a consumer transaction`
    AND NOT `the goods or services were intended for business use`

-- s 40: where the transaction "is evidenced by a document provided by the supplier" and "a provision of the document is ambiguous, the
-- provision must be interpreted against the supplier."
GIVEN `the document was provided by the supplier` IS A BOOLEAN, `the provision is ambiguous` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the ambiguous provision read against the supplier` IF
        `the document was provided by the supplier`
    AND `the provision is ambiguous`
